<title>GERMANY: Rexrodt seeks German ruling on Bewag.</title>
<headline>Rexrodt seeks German ruling on Bewag.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German cartel office said economics minister Guenter Rexrodt had agreed to pass on to Brussels its request for jurisdiction on the sale of Berlin's stake in electric utility Bewag.</p>
<p>Berlin has agreed to sell its remaining 50.8 percent stake in Bewag for 2.95 billion marks to a group comprising Southern Co of the U.S., Veba and Viag.</p>
<p>But German cartel authorities are concerned that Veba's other activities in the Berlin region could give it a market-dominating position.  </p>
<p>Cartel office spokeswoman Elke Zeise said Rexrodt had signed the office's request and passed it along to European cartel authorities in Brussels.</p>
<p>The German office is concerned about Veba subsidiary Preussen Elektra, which already has a presence in the Berlin area.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
